enchantments.text:
The weapon records major breakthroughs survived by its attuned bearer.
When the bearer successfully completes a Realm breakthrough while attuned to the weapon, choose one of the following permanent improvements, subject to the weapon’s normal grade limits:
- increase one enchantment’s additional damage die by one step, to a maximum of d10;
- increase one enchantment’s forced movement by 5 feet;
- increase one enchantment’s range by 10 feet;
- grant the weapon +1 to saving throws against being damaged, suppressed, or broken.
The same improvement cannot be selected more than twice.
This enchantment can record no more than three successful Realm breakthroughs unless the weapon becomes an Immortal Artifact.

The weapon becomes a personal Dao vessel.
When this enchantment is created, choose one existing Minor or Major enchantment on the weapon as its **Core Expression**.
The Core Expression gains one of the following improvements:
- its additional damage increases by 1d8;
- its forced movement increases by 10 feet;
- its range increases by 30 feet;
- one target affected by it has Disadvantage on its first saving throw against it each Long Rest;
- its CP cost is reduced by 1, to a minimum of 0, whenever the Core Expression is activated.
The chosen improvement must be written into the final weapon entry.
The weapon can later receive bespoke growth through Dao Insights, Realm breakthroughs, unique materials, or item-spirit awakening, but every new function must remain mechanically explicit and thematically connected to the Core Expression.
